### Python Guidelines for CTU

- Prefer explicit, descriptive names; avoid 1–2 letter identifiers.
- Guard clauses over deep nesting; avoid unnecessary try/except blocks.
- Keep comments minimal; explain only non-obvious rationale or invariants.
- Respect existing formatting; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Use tuple ordering carefully for image shapes `(height, width)` and OpenCV size `(width, height)`.
- Handle images via OpenCV consistently; read paths from the rule of thumb in [ctu/cocout_wrapper.py](mdc:ctu/cocout_wrapper.py).
- Validate dict keys for `modif_step_di` before use; treat as input contract.
- Maintain type clarity even without annotations; name variables to communicate intent.

